  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I minted Harbor Desk, but it stopped at the keys step. Everything I could do without you is done; the deploy and tests come after the keys.\n\n**Done:**\n- I saved your brief to `briefs/harbor_desk.md` and created the app (`harbor_desk`). It's set up to go on Vercel, with the Harbor Pilots workspace, the owner and two members, web search on and browser off. It's the standard app with nothing custom added.\n- The Harbor Desk name and colour #0B6E4F are applied.\n\n**Where it stopped:** six keys for outside services aren't set: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. I tried copying them from your live app `beta_app`, but this machine won't read saved keys off Vercel, so nothing was copied and nothing was left on disk. You'll need to type them in yourself.\n\n**What I need from you first: your Cloudflare account ID.** The app uses Cloudflare to store files, so it can't go live without this.\n\n1. Open a **second terminal** on the factory machine. Don't use this chat, because anything typed here ends up in the conversation.\n2. From the factory folder, run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n3. It tells you where to find the value. In short: sign in at https://dash.cloudflare.com and copy the **Account ID** shown on your account's overview page.\n4. Paste it at the prompt and press Enter.\n\nThis takes about two minutes. What you type stays hidden on screen, only goes to the app's settings on Vercel, and isn't saved in any file here or shown in this chat.\n\nTell me when it's done and I'll ask for the next key, one at a time. Once all six are in, the next step is the first deploy (about 10 minutes), and I'll ask for your yes before starting it.",
